From: Tai Ci maintainers
Subject: [PATCH] Do not resolve a function whose byte code buffer failed

The parser records allocation failures as a sticky DynBuf error on
fd->byte_code and keeps parsing. When a single allocation fails and later
ones succeed, the parse can finish and js_create_function() ran
resolve_variables()/resolve_labels() over the truncated buffer: skip_dead_code
read past it (SIGSEGV) and update_label() hit its label assertion for the -1
returned by new_label(). js_create_function() now reports out of memory
before resolving.

Upstream quickjs-ng df836d1 contains the defect.
Found by the one-failure mode of Tai's runtime.js compile sweep
(tests/test_quickjs_oom.c).
---
--- a/quickjs.c
+++ b/quickjs.c
@@ -37022,6 +37022,13 @@
     }
 #endif
 
+    /* the parser records allocation failures in the byte code buffer and
+       keeps going; never resolve a truncated buffer */
+    if (dbuf_error(&fd->byte_code)) {
+        JS_ThrowOutOfMemory(ctx);
+        goto fail;
+    }
+
     if (resolve_variables(ctx, fd))
         goto fail;
 
